{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01442",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 4.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.08,
      "end_seconds": 8.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "of course, leave it there how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.19,
      "end_seconds": 16.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.55,
      "end_seconds": 22.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.83,
      "end_seconds": 29.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "I've been dealing with pain going to my right shoulder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.89,
      "end_seconds": 34.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "so, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.86,
      "end_seconds": 45.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "It's, It's been going on for five days. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.11,
      "end_seconds": 48.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "alright, how frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.25,
      "end_seconds": 57.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.3,
      "end_seconds": 65.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.97,
      "end_seconds": 70.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "It's every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.25,
      "end_seconds": 81.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "let me think, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 81.81,
      "end_seconds": 88.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.18,
      "end_seconds": 100.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "Erm, I was getting to that! I've also had sharp pain in the upper right of my tummy. Oh, and bloating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.04,
      "end_seconds": 104.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.63,
      "end_seconds": 111.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "maybe a six out of ten on a bad day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 111.91,
      "end_seconds": 115.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.13,
      "end_seconds": 119.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "has there been any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.46,
      "end_seconds": 121.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 123.92,
      "end_seconds": 129.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.7,
      "end_seconds": 136.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.77,
      "end_seconds": 149.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you had any dark urine, weight loss or yellow eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.38,
      "end_seconds": 164.98,
      "duration_seconds": 14.6,
      "text": "Uh, no, no dark urine, no weight loss, no yellow eyes. I did have nausea after meals at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.61,
      "end_seconds": 169.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "have you had any pale stools or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.97,
      "end_seconds": 173.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "no, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.68,
      "end_seconds": 179.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.58,
      "end_seconds": 183.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.2,
      "end_seconds": 187.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.07,
      "end_seconds": 191.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "nothing on the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.86,
      "end_seconds": 194.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.78,
      "end_seconds": 198.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.58,
      "end_seconds": 201.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.99,
      "end_seconds": 209.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.5,
      "end_seconds": 235.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.11,
      "end_seconds": 242.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "No, um, not that that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.57,
      "end_seconds": 246.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.59,
      "end_seconds": 252.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I had a caesarean for my second baby nine years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.48,
      "end_seconds": 268.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "So, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.24,
      "end_seconds": 277.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "I, I have high cholesterol. I've had an underactive thyroid for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.38,
      "end_seconds": 283.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "So, does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.6,
      "end_seconds": 287.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.0,
      "end_seconds": 292.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.92,
      "end_seconds": 303.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "Oh, you know, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.97,
      "end_seconds": 307.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.37,
      "end_seconds": 323.07,
      "duration_seconds": 14.7,
      "text": "For my cholesterol, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Let me think, I'm on thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 324.95,
      "end_seconds": 335.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the thyroxine was 37.5 micrograms. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.37,
      "end_seconds": 340.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "hm do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.84,
      "end_seconds": 347.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "So, I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.98,
      "end_seconds": 351.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "let me quickly check your readings"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.6,
      "end_seconds": 362.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.95,
      "end_seconds": 393.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 75 beats a minute, respiratory rate 16, BP is 118 over 69. And temperature is 36.7 degrees, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.01,
      "end_seconds": 397.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "is that that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.16,
      "end_seconds": 400.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.72,
      "end_seconds": 407.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "So, now I'm gonna do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.17,
      "end_seconds": 411.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.99,
      "end_seconds": 432.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "There is tenderness under the right ribs when you breathe in, and no yellowing of the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.22,
      "end_seconds": 462.4,
      "duration_seconds": 27.18,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Having listened and examined, I don't have a clear answer today: biliary colic from gallstones is possible, and so is pancreatitis. I'm gonna order liver blood tests, for upper abdominal pain. I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the tummy for right upper quadrant pain. Let's use diclofenac, 50 milligrams, three times a day if needed, for three days. That's for gallbladder pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.22,
      "end_seconds": 466.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "thank you, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.27,
      "end_seconds": 474.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "keep meals small and low in fat until we have the scan we'll refer you to the surgeons"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 476.05,
      "end_seconds": 479.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "hmm, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.89,
      "end_seconds": 494.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 495.52,
      "end_seconds": 499.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I, I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 499.99,
      "end_seconds": 506.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "do get help quickly if you develop a fever, yellow eyes or severe constant pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 507.98,
      "end_seconds": 509.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 510.9,
      "end_seconds": 514.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "let's plan a check after the ultrasound"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 515.67,
      "end_seconds": 519.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Mm, I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 521.72,
      "end_seconds": 525.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "okay, that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 527.3,
      "end_seconds": 529.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 530.66,
      "end_seconds": 531.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}